# Commit After Completed Work

When working in this project and the workspace is a git repo, treat completed changes, bug fixes, and updates as needing a commit unless the user explicitly says not to.

Before committing:
- Run `git status`, `git diff`, and recent `git log` to understand all changes and commit style.
- Commit only files relevant to the completed task.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` files, credentials, local artifacts, or unrelated user changes.
- If unrelated changes are present, leave them unstaged.
- Run the relevant checks/tests when practical and mention any that were skipped.

Create a concise commit message that describes the outcome and why it matters. Do not push unless the user explicitly asks.
